  message: "DONE in PR #2329 for 8 of the 9 rows; the ninth (servant.yaml base_class ^Application$) is wrong as written and is filed, not fixed. Each analyzer part was built by an Opus subagent in its own worktree and reviewed; numbers are dev a5b3cca93 vs the branch.\nSCALA (http4s IOApp.Simple): scala.py records dotted, projected and parenthesised parent types (it read only a bare identifier). tapir: 6 objects extending IOApp.Simple get the entrypoint concept, 5 become main_function entries (the sixth is under a test path). Edges +24 extends, +5 implements, +30 dispatches_to, +7 and -1 calls; the -1/+1 pair is a wrong overload pick by the inherited-calls linker, exposed by the new parents (filed).\nHASKELL (yesod x2): an instance symbol records its class in meta.base_classes. haskellers: Yesod App is a hosted_application entry; YesodPersist and YesodAuth instances get database and auth.\nLUA (openresty lapis): lua.py emits a class symbol for X = R:extend(...) / :subclass(...) and a file-scope variable with constructed_from for X = C(...), a require alias read through. One row ADDED for the instance form (local app = lapis.Application()), which is what Kong uses; a lapis -> openresty alias so a Lapis-only project loads the file. kong: 3 applications, each read in source; +308 variable nodes.\nR (plumber x2, shiny) and F# (giraffe/saturn application): each records one caller-position usage context per call. Their rows are limited to position ^caller$; rows whose subject is a handler argument (plumber routes, filters, serializer; giraffe routes) are marked CANNOT FIRE, and giraffe's response writers moved from middleware to response, because fired on the caller they minted wrong entries. No Shiny, Plumber, Giraffe or Saturn repository is on this machine: these four are measured on fixtures only.\nCORE, NEEDED FOR THE ABOVE: a usage row now matches only calls written in its framework file's language. Before it, an R function calling its own createServer() gained a Node route from node-http.yaml. Regression check on cowboy, ghostfolio, flask-restful, alertmanager, apollo-server, chatwoot and pretix src/pretix: no concept, entry, edge or node change.\nNOT FIXED: servant.yaml:90. WAI's Application is a type synonym; a Servant app is a binding declared :: Application, and haskell.py records no declared type a row could read. No stable id moved on any of 19 trees.\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/three_pr_plan_11222026/pr2/RESULTS.md.\n\nFILED FROM THIS: WI-kibav (the Servant row and the other type-named rows), WI-potub (handler-argument contexts for R and F#), WI-hafif (inherited-calls overloads), WI-vubuj (Lua forms), WI-kovoj (Haskell leftovers), WI-zuton (definition rows are not language-gated)."  # d573
